1530524.description:
Original ID: 14
Original Title: Assign both Primary and Secondary WAN IPv6 address through PPPoEv6
Original Description: This test case is to verify that both primary and secondary WAN IPv6 address can be assigned through PPPoEv6 successfully.&#160;

1530530.steps:
1. Network-&gt;interface x1,set it zone WAN ,and select IP Assignment as PPPoE, then click OK
2. Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, fill in appropriate username, password and service name, select PPPoEv6 address Assignment as DHCPv6 Automatic mode, accept default settings for all other options, and click OK;
3. Protocol-&gt;PPPoE Client Settings,check Inactivity Disconnect,and accept default setting (10 minutes)
4.keep SonicWALL inactive for 10 minutes without any ipv4 and ipv6 traffic from LAN-&gt;WAN; 5.keep SonicWALL inactive for 10 minutes without ipv4 but ipv6 traffic from LAN-&gt;WAN; 6.keep SonicWALL inactive for 10 minutes without ipv6 but ipv4 traffic from LAN-&gt;WAN;

1530554.result:
in step 3&amp;4, regardless of flag M&amp;O,it will get Autonomous ipv6 address;
in step 5,traffic from LAN to WAN should be able to pass through
in step 6,the traffic from DUT to WAN should be OK ,From the captured packet,it should use WAN ipv6 address

1530553.description:
Original ID: 24
Original Title: Verify PPPoEv6 can obtain IPv6 address in DHCPv6 Rapid Commit mode 
Original Description: This test case is to verify PPPoEv6 can obtain IPv6 address in DHCPv6 Rapid Commit mode&#160;

1530534.steps:
1. Network-&gt;interface x1,set it zone WAN ,and select IP Assignment as PPPoE, then click OK
2. Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, fill in appropriate username, password and service name, select PPPoEv6 address Assignment as DHCPv6 Automatic mode, accept default settings for all other options, and click OK;
3. Protocol-&gt;PPPoE Client Settings,check Inactivity Disconnect,and accept default setting (10 minutes)
4. verify from the GUI that primary WAN can receive correct IPv6 address; 5.keep SonicWALL inactive for 10 minutes without any traffic from LAN-&gt;WAN; verify that PPPoE connection is terminated; 6.explicitly re-connect PPPoEv6 through management GUI; verify that PPPoEv6 connection got re-established; 7.keep SonicWALL inactive for another 10 minutes without any traffic from LAN-&gt;WAN; 8.then send IPv6 traffic from LAN to WAN,&#65533;verify that PPPoEv6 connection got re-established;&#65533;

